  "copy": {
    "series_title": "The Stories Behind the Trier Beer Festival 2026",
    "caption": "Thirty years of brewing experience, and a project of his own: meet Still Brewing Society, the next feature in The Stories Behind the Trier Beer Festival 2026.\n\nOn 7–8 August 2026, Still Brewing Society appeared at the Bingen Bier Festival in Bingen am Rhein. The organiser introduced it as Andi Dietrich’s own project, following his appearance with Brauquadrat the previous year. Behind the new name is a brewer with around three decades of experience across different breweries.\n\nNow @still.brewing.society is on the lineup for the Trier Beer Festival on 2–3 October 2026 at Blesius Garten, Trier, hosted by @kraft_braeu_trier and @blesius_garten.\n\nExplore the Bingen milestone on Beer Chronicles through the link in the accompanying Story.\n\nTickets are still available:\nhttps://www.ticket-regional.de/events_info.php?eventID=275224\n\n#BeerChronicles #TrierBeerFestival #StillBrewingSociety #CraftBeer #BeerHistory",
    "story_text": "BEER CHRONICLES\nThe Stories Behind the Trier Beer Festival 2026\nStill Brewing Society\n2026\nStill Brewing Society appears at the Bingen Bier Festival.\nTRIER BEER FESTIVAL · 2–3 OCTOBER 2026 · BLESIUS GARTEN\nTickets still available — see feed caption\nbeer-chronicles.org",
    "alt_text": "Cream poster with centred charcoal serif lettering and fine copper rules. At the top: “BEER CHRONICLES” and “The Stories Behind the Trier Beer Festival 2026”. The original Still Brewing Society logo has irregular cream lettering on a charcoal square. Below it: “2026” in copper and “Still Brewing Society appears at the Bingen Bier Festival.” The footer reads “TRIER BEER FESTIVAL · 2–3 OCTOBER 2026 · BLESIUS GARTEN”, followed by “beer-chronicles.org”."
  },
